very eval (V/T/R clean vs recovery ± SD, detection)\n- Table 2: Cross-model comparison (Qwen 5s vs LLaMA 3s)\n- Table 3: LLaMA per-seed breakdown\n- Table 4: Scale ablation (500 vs 2500 traj)\n- Table 5: Diminishing returns in gap reduction\n- Table 6: Few-shot recovery prompting\n- Table 7: Per-operator analysis (exploratory)\n- Figure 1: Power curve\n\n## Experiment Design Reference (from review_context.yaml)\n\nThe experimental design document lists 6 imagined experiments:\n1. Recovery Eval Multi-Seed (5-seed × 3 conditions) → Covered in Table 1\n2. LLaMA Cross-Model Replication (3-seed) → Covered in Tables 2-3\n3. Scale Ablation (25K–50K trajectories) → Covered in Tables 4-5\n4. Recovery Prompting (Few-Shot) → Covered in Table 6\n5. Per-Operator Deep Dive (Multi-Seed) → Covered in Table 7\n6. Scale-Up Data Collection → Covered in Appendix B\n\nAll 6 imagined experiments are present in the paper. Coverage is complete.\n\n## Your Review Task\n\nEvaluate the paper on:\n1. **Experimental methodology**: Are conditions properly controlled? Are comparisons fair? Is the evaluation protocol sound?\n2. **Statistical rigor**: Are tests appropriate? Is the honesty about power/significance appropriate or does it undermine claims?\n3. **Data volume confound**: Vanilla=4358 samples, TaxEI/Random=9029. How much does this matter?\n4. **Cross-model validity**: n=3 seeds on LLaMA — does this add value or is it too weak?\n5. **Scale ablation interpretation**: Does 29% gap reduction at 5× scale undermine the task-structure hypothesis?\n6. **Missing experiments or controls**: What's absent that would strengthen claims?\n7. **Reproducibility**: Is there enough detail to replicate?\n\nProduce a structured review with:\n- Summary (2-3 sentences)\n- Strengths (numbered list)\n- Weaknesses (numbered list, with severity: major/minor)\n- Questions for Authors (numbered)\n- Missing Experiments / Suggestions\n- Score (1-6) with justification\n- Confidence (1-5)\n\nBe rigorous but fair. This i